            "success": "1771739574446"
          },
          "code": "INPROGRESS_NEGOTIATIONS_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1771738926219",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771738926222_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a Supplier Negotiations Advisor that will analyze negotiation information to determine those negotiations that are at risk. use the information in the following negotiation lists:\n\nActive negotiations that are closing soon with insufficient participation: {{$context.$nodes.GET_ACTIVE_NEGOTIATIONS.$output.items}}\nNegotiations approved after the open date: {{$context.$nodes.GET_APPROVED_NOT_PUBLISHED_NEGOTIATIONS.$output.items}}\nPaused negotiations: {{$context.$nodes.GET_PAUSED_NEGOTIATIONS.$output.items}}\n\n#Analysis Criteria Rules (Priority)\n-Active negotiation closing soon with insufficient participation (Maximum 2 negotiations). Take the ones closest to closing.\n-Negotiations approved after open date. Take the ones that was approved the longest.\n-Paused negotiations. \n-Active negotiation closing soon (more than 1 day) with insufficient participation. Take the ones closest to closing.\n\nUsing the priority rules and attributes to reciew, analyze all the negotiation lists, don't display this in output and don't reveal any analysis or list the negotiations. Then return a concise, urgency-ranked list of those needing attention, order the list by urgency.  You MUST include at least one negotiation for each list but the output list must have only the top 5 negotiations at risk (no more).\n\n#FINAL OUTPUT\nUsing your previous analysis, for summarization, write exactly one friendly, plain-language sentence that explains why these negotiations are requiring attention, don't include specific information about the negotiations and don't list the ranked negotiations. You can include the most critical negotiation requiring attention. Your putput must use the language specified in the formatting rules.\n\n#Formatting Rules For Output\n -Must Generate the content in {{$context.$variables.Language}} language.\n -Output ONLY brief summary (no more than 100 words).\n -Do NOT include negotiation names, numbers, dates, counts, scores, or any specific fields.\n -Must refer to the item as \"negotiations\", don't use any other term.\n -Show all monetary amounts in {{$context.$variables.Currency}} currency and format the currency using {{$context.$variables.NumberFormat}} formatting style (for example, symbol placement, decimal separators, etc.).\n -Format all dates using {{$context.$variables.DateFormat}} date format and if there is time you can use this {{$context.$variables.TimeFormat}} time format."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
